<speak>That is exactly what happened on the last trip. I came home with a folder full of booking printouts, receipts, and a personal letter I had meant to file before leaving. Then everything sat on the sideboard because I did not feel like sorting it after travelling. My wife eventually asked whether the folder was part of the furniture now. This time I will leave the personal paperwork in its proper place before we go. I might bring a small notebook for things I remember, but not the whole collection of loose papers. A holiday should not require carrying a miniature office in my bag.</speak>